61f162b5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ef9e943fcda0768af743da26c0dc15479be2fd9c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider a feedback system with characteristic equation <img src=\"/media/dd87f050bade8485cc87f0e87eefa4cc8cedeade.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The angles of the asymptotes of the root-locus branches with the real axis of the s-plane is/are ______ . (Assume that <em>K</em> varies from 0 to 84).</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 60°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 180°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 300°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 45°</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/359ed7026c61bcdbf122bc8baa33a6b310f5de1f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/17060f2b17999fc883a3eb69b2f60509bd9c4661.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a unity feedback ac position control system is <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/f164723c87be37c3246a116d02d39b3ade169550.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> the input shaft rotates at <img src=\"/media/624ced8ae59530144b7244381f7e498144c49967.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> revolution per second, the steady-state velocity error is 0.2°, the value of damping factor is ________ . </p>\n<p>(Answer upto three decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.052","high":"0.052"},"solution":"<p>0.052 (0.045 to 0.060)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3da6cfcb291ae05d8dc1f89f198b04dd714aa429.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6ba980967988ac48622bfff6cfbbe16fdfbd2429.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A closed loop servo is represented by the differential equation <img src=\"/media/0f3c6fe2af4faea0ae53423e31bd5aa53ea4efae.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> where ‘<em>c</em>’ is the displacement of the output shaft, ‘<em>r</em>’ is the displacement of the input shaft and <em>e</em> = <em>r</em> – <em>c</em>. The percentage peak overshoot for unit step input is ________ %. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"21.55","high":"21.55"},"solution":"<p>21.55 (21.40 to 21.65)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/99b1f03d4042a13f153c87214a5924f06379808f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/de1786fb3fafbf214deddc1789c31933dbfb85d6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<p> </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A unity negative feedback control system has open loop transfer function given by G(s)H(s) =<img src=\"/media/648c698de0772081b9045281f67f2bdd6a63f2dc.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> . The constant ‘λ’ is defined as, <img src=\"/media/010ce428c20ff51a0109e7702c6e8cdc5329e6aa.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is the angle of departure. If the angle of departure, <img src=\"/media/148cf3fab4c0c98927554c824732564f0538d085.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is for the complex pole in II-quandrant is then the absolute value off the consant ‘λ’ is ________ . (Round off to the nearest integer).</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"202","high":"202"},"solution":"<p>202 (200 - 204)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6093aaaf98de95d743a19f2274be6533e7fdd1af.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider a unity negative feedback control sy